 ## Overview
-The Time-Sliced Pipelined Architecture is a hardware design methodology for volume rendering systems that achieves real-time performance by overlapping the execution of distinct pipeline stages through time-slicing [S1, unofficial]. It solves the bottleneck of sequential processing in traditional volume rendering pipelines by allowing multiple tasks to be processed simultaneously on shared or replicated functional blocks [S1, unofficial]. Unlike general-purpose DSP-based solutions, this architecture integrates the rendering pipeline into a unified multi-core structure, enabling continuous hardware-software communication and interactive frame rates [S1, unofficial].
+The Time-Sliced Pipelined Architecture is a hardware design methodology for volume rendering that achieves real-time performance by overlapping distinct pipeline stages through time-slicing [S1, unofficial]. It solves sequential processing bottlenecks by allowing multiple tasks to run simultaneously on shared or replicated functional blocks, enabling continuous hardware-software communication and interactive frame rates [S1, unofficial].
 
